      "content": "Those details you shared sound like a serious escalation of workplace behavior that requires immediate, careful action. Before guessing about legal claims or filing complaints, it is crucial to document every instance objectively with dates, times, and direct quotes (where possible) while continuing to perform your daily duties professionally. Consult with a local employment lawyer or your HR department at the very next chance to discuss these specific events, as they can guide you on the correct legal channels and ensure your documentation holds up under scrutiny. Attempting to confront management with accusations alone without verified legal advice can sometimes backfire if the situation turns sour during the investigation.",
